# Defaults for the validation job (packages/job). Committed; holds no secrets. The process environment wins over every
# line here. The contract with the Builder: docs/builder-integration.md

# The work queue the job drains (the Builder's validation requests). Region and credentials come from the task role;
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_SQS points it at a local queue for development.
# WORK_QUEUE_URL=
# Items' files come from <BUILDER_CONTENT_URL>/v1/storage/contents/<hash>; the result goes to
# <BUILDER_CALLBACK_URL>/v1/collections/<id>/validation-result, signed with BUILDER_CALLBACK_SECRET (a secret, never here).
# BUILDER_CONTENT_URL=https://builder-api.decentraland.org
# BUILDER_CALLBACK_URL=https://builder-api.decentraland.org
# BUILDER_CALLBACK_SECRET=
# One item's files together may not exceed this many bytes: 32 MB.
MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=33554432

# Slack: one message per collection in the channel, edited to its verdict, and one thread reply per item (every finding,
# the model's summary, the thumbnail and the worn views) — the only record, since the job keeps nothing. The app needs
# chat:write and files:write and must be in the channel. Unset, nothing is posted.
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# SLACK_CHANNEL=

# The model credential: a `claude setup-token` (sk-ant-oat…); a secret, never here. Unset, items still render, but the
# visual checks that ask the model are not answered.
# ANTHROPIC_OAUTH_SETUP_TOKEN=

# The render server (the Unity avatar scene as a Linux player drawing on the CPU): the command that starts it, the build
# it is (release and sha256) and a folder both it and the job can reach. The Docker image sets all three; unset, the
# job runs it in Docker through render-server-docker.sh (a laptop).
# RENDER_SERVER=
# RENDER_SERVER_BUILD=
# RENDER_SERVER_WORK_DIR=<tmp>/wearable-validator-native

# The job exits after this many empty long polls in a row, or once its runtime budget is spent.
# EMPTY_RECEIVES_TO_EXIT=2
# MAX_RUNTIME_MINUTES=55
# How long a received collection stays hidden from other tasks; the job extends it while the collection is in hand.
# VISIBILITY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800

# json for one JSON line per event (the image sets it); anything else prints readable lines.
# LOG_FORMAT=json
